Classification Justification

SO-F-005 defines the capability required to transform an approved adaptive decision into corresponding vehicle action and to provide relevant execution-state information.

It is derived from SO-F-001 and operates downstream of the decision-generation capability established by SO-F-004.

Its responsibility begins only after the applicable authorization boundary has been satisfied.

---

Operational Role

SO-F-005 occupies the execution stage of the current adaptive processing flow:

Operating Context
       ↓
Decision Generation
       ↓
Generated Decision
       ↓
Authorization
       ↓
Approved Decision
       ↓
Action Execution
       ↓
Execution State

---

Classification Boundaries

SO-F-005 shall remain distinct from:

- Environmental perception.
- Operating-context interpretation.
- Adaptive decision generation.
- Decision authorization.
- Physical system design and implementation details.
- Independent selection of a new adaptive response.

---

Classification Notes

- Derived from SO-F-001.
- Operationally follows SO-F-004.
- Receives an approved decision rather than an unapproved generated decision.
- Represents the execution stage of the current adaptive processing architecture.
- Includes observation and reporting of execution state where required.
- Does not establish decision authority.
- Does not establish the authorization mechanism.
- Does not establish the final destination of execution feedback.
- Future execution-related objectives shall maintain traceability to SO-F-005.
